protocol was completed on both nodes: each had a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity corroborated by fixed lifecycle observations, and recovered service, data, networking, and end-to-end UDP behavior.","limitations":["The fixed after-executor listening-socket observation for node1 was empty, which conflicts with repeated executor netstat output showing UDP 9098 active shortly before the snapshot. This lowers confidence slightly, although post-reboot service status and end-to-end receipt strongly support functionality.","Systemd failed-service inspection was unsupported on this legacy SysV platform, so there is no independent global failed-service inventory.","The lifecycle snapshots do not include a final application-directory inventory; retention of collector.py.pre-repair is inferred from its creation and the absence of any later removal in the complete command timeline."]}
